{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-V13S-RESULT.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The one-time v13s paid re-send (D753, D754): result\n     2\t\n     3\t**Verdict: STOP (complete).** The verdict is sealed in `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23/verdict.json`, with the readings in\n     4\t`readings.json` and the key in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/`.\n     5\t\n     6\t- **Joint:** usable in 3 of 9 pairs against the registered 8 of 9; per snapshot old-1 2, old-2 1, old-3 0.\n     7\t- **Separate:** usable in 0 of 9 pairs.\n     8\t- **Published defects:** 5, all singleton \"deciding gaps\".\n     9\t- Nothing is tuned on these 36 answers (`PAID-GATE.md` §5).\n    10\t\n    11\t## 1. The run\n    12\t\n    13\t- **Model and plan.** gpt-6-luna (poc-v118's judging setting). The plan is `paid-plan-v13s.json` (`0dc7c310…`): 12 requests × 3\n    14\t  draws, the D751 request.\n    15\t- **Spend.** $0.3339 of the $0.50 cap (ledger), with no stop. All 36 scored first attempts finished, and the 22 diagnostic retries\n    16\t  were sent after them.\n    17\t- **Code decisions on the scored first attempts:**\n    18\t\n    19\t  | Arm | Published | Refused |\n    20\t  |---|---:|---:|\n    21\t  | Joint (9) | 3 | 6 |\n    22\t  | Separate (18) | 5 | 13 |\n    23\t  | Singletons (9) | 6 | 3 |\n    24\t\n    25\t  - The separate arm's pairs: 8 not reconciled, 1 refused.\n    26\t  - After the diagnostic retries (not scored): joint 3 published, separate 11, singletons 8.\n    27\t\n    28\t## 2. Why the code refused 22 first attempts (each read against its source)\n    29\t\n    30\tEvery one of the 22 refused answers contains at least one error of luna's against a rule the request states. None was refused by a\n    31\tcheck alone.\n    32\t\n    33\t| Class (answers can carry several) | Count |\n    34\t|---|---:|\n    35\t| A piece of a longer expression copied (e.g. \"$108.0 billion\" from \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\", the schema's own example) | 8 |\n    36\t| Reference marking missing or doubled (S5) | 6 |\n    37\t| More than one figure marked as the outcome (S6) | 4 |\n    38\t| A qualifier or extra words inside the number (\"around $113 billion to $114 billion\") | 4 |\n    39\t| Not as written (a range rewritten with a dash; \"$1 billion\") | 2 |\n    40\t| A table number split by a line break (\"$\" and \"177,837\" on separate lines). The check is strict here; it appeared twice, both times beside a model error | 2 |\n    41\t| A qualifier mismatch (\"over\" recorded as \"more than\") | 1 |\n    42\t| Value and range both given (S7) | 1 |\n    43\t\n    44\t- **The check-strictness case** (a number split by a line break in a table) is real and worth fixing, but it decided no outcome here.\n    45\t\n    46\t## 3. What the readers found (two blind families, a third Codex reader on 12 disagreements)\n    47\t\n    48\t- **Usable pairs.** Joint 3 of 9 against separate 0 of 9, a gain of 3. The registered pass needs at least 8 joint pairs.\n    49\t- **The five published defects** are all singleton deciding gaps: an unsized adjustment decides the band.\n    50\t\n    51\t  | Packet | Case | Draw | The adjustment |\n    52\t  |---|---|---|---|\n    53\t  | P15 | O | 2 | half of a possible investment counted, with no evidence for the fraction; the full amount moves the answer to the next band |\n    54\t  | P16 | E | 1 | growth cut to 90%, taking FY2028 below $40B, with no passage sizing the loss |\n    55\t  | P19 | S (CY2027) | 2 | a data-center share of at least five-sixths needed for the band; no passage establishes it |\n    56\t  | P26 | S (CY2027) | 1 | an Oracle deduction the passages do not bound decides between bands |\n    57\t  | P27 | S (CY2027) | 3 | a 75% share gives one band and a 95% share another; the passages do not say which is likelier |\n    58\t- **Luna on E.** It answered three times with no \"can't tell yet\":\n    59\t  - d1: $38B, rung 3, an unsized cut, a defect;\n    60\t  - d2: $43B, rung 2;\n    61\t  - d3: $37.5B, an unsized cut, refused for format.\n    62\t\n    63\t  Its behaviour on E matches the free tests' Claude writer, not the Codex writer.\n    64\t\n    65\t## 4. What it shows, and what it does not\n    66\t\n    67\t- **The design point (D725), directional.** Computing the pair together gave 3 usable pairs, and computing them apart gave none,\n    68\t  because separate answers did not reconcile. That supports the design idea, but far below the registered line, on one run.\n    69\t- **The production model on this format.**\n    70\t  - Luna fails mechanical format rules on 61% of first attempts. The diagnostic retries show many are fixable once named.\n    71\t  - On boundary questions it publishes numbers decided by unsized adjustments: 5 of its 6 published scored singletons.\n    72\t  - The free tests' proxy writers (Claude, Codex) did not predict either rate.\n    73\t- **Not shown.** Whether a stronger model, a higher reasoning effort, or code-side format repair would pass. Each is a separate\n    74\t  decision and a separate test.\n     1\t# judging-v13 paid gate: plan, harness and reading rule (registered before any send; D725, D729, D730)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result (D733): STOP.** All 72 answers were refused, and $0.3677 was spent; see `PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`.\n     4\t\n     5\t## 1. What is sent\n     6\t\n     7\t`paid_gate.py plan paid-plan.json` builds 12 requests from the stored runs.\n     8\t\n     9\t| Unit | Arm | Members | Evidence shown |\n    10\t|---|---|---|---|\n    11\t| pair-old-1 (09-20: v4 total, v8 Data Center) | joint; separate-v4; separate-v8 | both; one; one | the union of both stored requests' evidence in view (237 items), in every arm |\n    12\t| pair-old-2 (v14, v9) | joint; separate-v14; separate-v9 | as above | 237 |\n    13\t| pair-old-3 (v3, v35) | joint; separate-v3; separate-v35 | as above | 260 |\n    14\t| single-O (old-2 v29, equity commitments) | single | v29 | its own request's (35) |\n    15\t| single-S (old-2 v6, four hyperscalers' 2027 capex) | single | v6 | 31 |\n    16\t| single-E (old-3 v41, FY2028 Vera CPU) | single | v41 | 15 |\n    17\t\n    18\t- **Each request:** judging-v13's system text (`judging-v13-draft.txt`, 4,373 characters); the family header with the exact outcome\n    19\t  keys; the evidence; the themes once. No earlier forecast is shown (D728). The strict v13 schema.\n    20\t- **The model:** poc-v118's re-judging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens).\n    21\t- **Draws:** three per request, so 36 first attempts.\n    22\t- **Retry:** a calculation the checks refuse, or a schema-invalid answer, is retried once with the reasons. A second refusal makes the\n    23\t  unit unresolved.\n    24\t- **What is scored:** the first attempt, on both arms (§3f). Retries are sent and recorded for diagnosis only.\n    25\t- **The separate arm:** its two first answers per pair and draw are merged and checked over the pair's family (C3, C4 across the two).\n    26\t\n    27\t## 2. Spend and stops\n    28\t\n    29\t- **The ledger:** one, at Alex's ceiling (`paid_gate.py send <folder> <ceiling> paid-plan.json` refuses any other ceiling).\n    30\t- **Budget:** the real budget transport and stop gate, which reserve each request's worst case before sending. After a stop, nothing\n    31\t  more is sent, and the remaining units are recorded as not sent.\n    32\t- **Estimate** (at `hivemind.model.PRICES`: gpt-6-luna, $0.10 input and $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as\n    33\t  characters / 4):\n    34\t  - a pair request is about 34–38k input tokens and a singleton 6–9k;\n    35\t  - the 36 first attempts cost about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n    36\t  - the transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request.\n    37\t  - **Proposed ceiling: $0.50.** It covers every scored attempt. Retries come last (§3g), so a ceiling stop among them leaves the\n    38\t    scored test complete.\n    39\t- **Sends:** one at a time, every first attempt before any retry (§3g). Each send has its own archive, so no draw is answered from\n    40\t  another.\n    41\t\n    42\t## 3. The $0 rehearsal (`paid_rehearsal.py`, `rehearsal.log`: 16 of 16)\n    43\t\n    44\t- **Clean run:** 36 first attempts, every HTTP body byte-equal to an independently built request, every unit published, the separate\n    45\t  arm reconciled in 9 of 9, the spend settled under the ceiling.\n    46\t- **Paths:**\n    47\t  - a refused calculation is retried, then published;\n    48\t  - two refusals give unresolved;\n    49\t  - a schema-invalid answer is retried;\n    50\t  - two separate answers that each pass alone are refused when reconciled (C3);\n    51\t  - after a ledger stop, nothing more is sent.\n    52\t- **Packets:** 27 packets with the arm hidden. The verdict is computed on synthetic readings: both arms good gives STOP (gain under 3);\n    53\t  a joint gain of 4 gives PASS; one published singleton defect gives STOP; a separate-arm defect alone does not stop; a missing\n    54\t  reading gives INCOMPLETE.\n    55\t\n    56\t## 3b. After council round 47 (`codex-r47.md`)\n    57\t\n    58\t- **[47.1] Reconciliation:** forecasts of the same quantity and scenario with equal recomputed values and bounds are unified before the\n    59\t  family's checks run. The duplicate's derivation is kept in results. Forecasts that differ stay as a conflict. Rehearsed: an agreeing\n    60\t  pair passes, and a disagreeing pair is refused (C4).\n    61\t- **[47.2] One authorization:**\n    62\t  - `paid-plan.sha256` pins the reviewed plan, and the sender refuses any other plan;\n    63\t  - `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json` is created exclusively at the first send, so a second launch is refused;\n    64\t  - (unit, arm) pairs are unique.\n    65\t- **[47.3] Every attempt recorded:**\n    66\t  - a `started` line is written before the provider is called;\n    67\t  - checker failures and arithmetic errors are refusals, recorded with the raw answer;\n    68\t  - every planned unit has a final status (`finals.json`), even after an abort;\n    69\t  - a refused reservation never reaches the provider.\n    70\t- **[47.4] Readings validated:** exact packets and cards, two readings (A, B) per card with yes or no and a ground for each question,\n    71\t  and a third reading on every disagreement. Otherwise the verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n    72\t- **[47.5] Packets:**\n    73\t  - the question text and ladder;\n    74\t  - each passage exactly as the request showed it, including those named only in `rests_on`;\n    75\t  - declared figures with renumbered ids, the recomputed outcomes and the recorded assumptions;\n    76\t  - the cards a non-reconciled separate unit has;\n    77\t  - neutral decision labels.\n    78\t- **Rehearsal:** 27 of 27 (`rehearsal.log`). The $0 gate still passes (`gate-run27.txt`: 87 of 87), and the mutants are unchanged.\n    79\t\n    80\t## 3c. After council round 47b (`codex-r47b.md`)\n    81\t\n    82\t- **[47b.1] Reconciliation:**\n    83\t  - Two recomputed values are the same when their bounds match and each end agrees within 1e-9 relative. A floating-point copy\n    84\t    unifies; a real difference stays a conflict.\n    85\t  - The readers never see the unified calculation. Each card of a reconciled packet is shown with its own original answer.\n    86\t- **[47b.2] Completeness comes from the attempt records.** `answers.jsonl` is the one record of what happened. For each planned unit\n    87\t  and draw, the final status is derived from it:\n    88\t  - no started line: **not sent**;\n    89\t  - a started line with no finished line: **interrupted**;\n    90\t  - a first refusal with no retry sent: **retry not sent**;\n    91\t  - otherwise, the last attempt's decision, and a second refusal is **unresolved**.\n    92\t\n    93\t  `results.json` is written from these records in a `finally`, so an abort still leaves it. The verdict is INCOMPLETE for every\n    94\t  status other than published, held or unresolved. That includes a reservation or HTTP failure, recorded as **transport**.\n    95\t- **[47b.3] Packets:**\n    96\t  - Every attempt of every card is listed, with neutral labels and check codes only.\n    97\t  - Each card is its own derivation: the figures its outcome and reference rest on, renumbered F1.. for that card alone.\n    98\t  - Its recorded assumptions are mapped to the same numbers. A record that names a figure outside the card is left out.\n    99\t- **[47b.4] Binding:**\n   100\t  - `packets.md` and the key are each created exclusively, once. A second `packets` call is refused.\n   101\t  - The key carries the run's digest (`answers.jsonl`, `results.json`, `plan.json`) and the sha256 of `packets.md`.\n   102\t  - The readings file carries the sha256 of the packets it was read on.\n   103\t  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE when any of the three differs, or when a ground is not a non-empty string naming a passage (e…) or a\n   104\t    figure (F…) of that packet.\n   105\t- **Rehearsal:** 41 of 41 (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   106\t  - a floating-point copy unifies;\n   107\t  - a reconciled card shows its own derivation;\n   108\t  - every attempt is listed;\n   109\t  - a transport failure makes the verdict INCOMPLETE;\n   110\t  - an interruption during a retry leaves results, marks the unit interrupted and the rest not sent;\n   111\t  - a retry that was never sent is incomplete;\n   112\t  - the card view maps assumption records and leaves out other cards';\n   113\t  - a second packets run, readings made on other packets, a run changed after freezing, and null or foreign grounds are each refused\n   114\t    or INCOMPLETE.\n   115\t- **Mutants:** 13 of 13 caught, and the control passes (`paid_mutants.py`, `paid-mutants.log`). Each mutant breaks one of these\n   116\t  defences on a scratch copy. The plan is unchanged (sha256 `6f81dae5…`), and `calc_check.py` is unchanged since gate run 27.\n   117\t\n   118\t## 3d. After council round 47c (`codex-r47c.md`)\n   119\t\n   120\t- **[47c.1] Reconciliation, by the joint arm's rule:**\n   121\t  - Only a forecast of a declared shared quantity is unified, and only with the other call's forecast of the same quantity and\n   122\t    scenario when their values are the same.\n   123\t  - Duplicates inside one call are never unified, so C3 and C4 judge them as they judge a joint answer.\n   124\t- **[47c.2] The key only orders the packets.**\n   125\t  - Each packet's decision, cards and allowed grounds come from the run.\n   126\t  - The verdict renders all packets again from the run and the key's order, and requires the text to equal `packets.md`, the key's\n   127\t    sha256 and the readings' sha256.\n   128\t  - The key must map exactly one packet to each unit of the run. A decision written into the key is ignored.\n   129\t- **[47c.3] Abstentions and attempts:**\n   130\t  - Each card is labelled K1, K2, … and is itself a valid ground, so a no-figure abstention can be read.\n   131\t  - Every earlier attempt shows its own answer, with figures named T<n>.F…. An attempt with no parsed answer shows its recorded\n   132\t    failure as a neutral label.\n   133\t  - Check codes are not shown: a cross-member code (C3, or C4 across members) occurs only in a joint answer and would reveal the arm.\n   134\t    The reasons stay in `results.json`.\n   135\t- **[47c.4] A torn journal:**\n   136\t  - A line that does not parse is skipped and listed as damaged. Its attempt counts as unfinished.\n   137\t  - `paid_gate.py recover <folder>` rebuilds `results.json` read-only and sends nothing.\n   138\t  - The verdict is INCOMPLETE while any line is damaged.\n   139\t- **Rehearsal:** 48 of 48, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   140\t  - two equal forecasts inside one answer, and two equal shared forecasts inside one call, are both refused after reconciliation, as\n   141\t    in a joint answer;\n   142\t  - an abstention reads with K1 as its ground;\n   143\t  - earlier attempts show their answers, with no codes;\n   144\t  - a key that maps packets to other units is INCOMPLETE;\n   145\t  - a decision written into the key changes nothing;\n   146\t  - a torn journal recovers with 35 units published and the torn one interrupted, and its verdict is INCOMPLETE.\n   147\t- **A rehearsal fault found and traced:** one parallel control run failed 47 of 48.\n   148\t  - The swap test exchanged P01 and P02. In about 2 of 26 shuffles, these are two draws of the same unit and arm.\n   149\t  - The rehearsal's draws answer alike, so their text is identical and the swap changes nothing.\n   150\t  - That is harmless to the verdict, which counts by unit, not by draw. The test now swaps two different units.\n   151\t- **Mutants:** 19 of 19 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   152\t  - Three missed in the first run and were traced:\n   153\t    - one was stale, because packets now render from the attempts;\n   154\t    - one was masked by the shared-only filter, and a shared within-call case was added;\n   155\t    - one disabled only half a condition.\n   156\t  - One mutant is equivalent and is left out: unifying any key across calls, not only declared shared ones. C3 looks only at\n   157\t    forecasts reachable from each member's own outcome, so the result does not change.\n   158\t\n   159\t## 3e. After council round 47d (`codex-r47d.md`): three structural rules\n   160\t\n   161\tRounds 47b to 47d kept finding the same two things: process information inside the readers' packets, and a mapping from packets to\n   162\tunits that could change after reading. These findings were answered by rule, not one by one.\n   163\t\n   164\t1. **The scoring text holds only what the four questions need.** For each card: the question, the ladder, the passages it names,\n   165\t   its own figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. It carries no attempt history, no code decision\n   166\t   and no check code. The verdict applies the code's decision itself.\n   167\t   - Earlier attempts go to `attempts.md`. That file is for diagnostic reading only and is never scored. Each attempt sits under its\n   168\t     own shuffled label (D01, …), with no link to a packet. [47d.3]\n   169\t   - A card with no final answer says why in plain words: no request was sent; the request was started and no answer was recorded;\n   170\t     no answer arrived; the answer was refused and its retry was not sent; or the answer did not match the format. [47d.4]\n   171\t2. **The text the readers receive commits to the mapping.** The key is {a random salt, the run's digest, the packet order, the\n   172\t   attempt labels}. Its sha256 is the first line of `packets.md`. The verdict refuses a key whose sha256 differs from that line. It\n   173\t   also renders the packets again from the run and the key, and refuses a mismatch with `packets.md` or with the readings' sha256.\n   174\t   A swap of two packets with identical text is caught, and so is a decision written into the key. [47d.1]\n   175\t3. **Reconciliation is one to one.** A declared shared forecast is unified only when each of the two calls holds exactly one\n   176\t   candidate for that quantity and scenario, and their values are the same. Otherwise every copy stays, for C3 and C4 to judge as in a\n   177\t   joint answer. [47d.2]\n   178\t\n   179\t- **The record:** an attempt that was started and not finished is kept in `results.json` as interrupted.\n   180\t- **Rehearsal:** 51 of 51, three times (`rehearsal.log`). The new cases:\n   181\t  - the scoring text has no attempt, decision or code;\n   182\t  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n   183\t  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n   184\t  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n   185\t  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n   186\t  - an interrupted card says the request was started.\n   187\t- **Mutants:** 20 of 20 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   188\t\n   189\t## 3f. After council round 47e (`codex-r47e.md`)\n   190\t\n   191\t- **[47e.1] The first attempt is scored, on both arms.**\n   192\t  - In the joint arm, a cross-card conflict (C3) is refused and retried with its reason, so the retry can repair it. In the separate\n   193\t    arm, the same conflict appears only when the two answers are reconciled, after both calls are over, and there is no retry.\n   194\t  - Scoring the final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have.\n   195\t  - D725 registered both arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about retries. Its pass and stop lines stay as\n   196\t    written and are applied to the first attempts.\n   197\t  - Retries are still sent and read for diagnosis (`attempts.md`), and are not counted.\n   198\t  - Rehearsed: the joint pair is published after its retry, but its refused first attempt is scored, so both arms come out at 6.\n   199\t- **[47e.2] One unit.** A shared forecast is unified only when the two copies have the same unit, as well as the same value and bounds.\n   200\t  Rehearsed: 110 USD bn against 110 USD is refused (C4).\n   201\t- **[47e.3] Every returned text is readable.**\n   202\t  - When the format check fails an answer, the scoring packet keeps its neutral label.\n   203\t  - The text the model returned, and the passages it names, go to `attempts.md` under a blind label. This covers both a first attempt\n   204\t    and a final one that fails the format.\n   205\t- **[47e.4] One verdict per run.**\n   206\t  - `verdict` copies the readings into the run once (`readings.json`, created exclusively).\n   207\t  - It scores them and writes `verdict.json` once, holding the readings' sha256, the key commitment, the packets' sha256, the run digest\n   208\t    and the result.\n   209\t  - A second verdict on the run is refused. `paid_gate.py replay` recomputes from the sealed readings and must reproduce the result.\n   210\t  - Rehearsed: the second verdict is refused; replay reproduces the result; after the sealed readings are edited, replay fails.\n   211\t- **Rehearsal:** 55 of 55, run three times (`rehearsal.log`).\n   212\t- **Mutants:** 25 of 25 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   213\t  - Two obsolete mutants were repointed or removed.\n   214\t  - One mutant crashed on a missing file and not on the defence. The test was corrected, and the mutant now fails the right check.\n   215\t\n   216\t## 3g. After council round 47f (`codex-r47f.md`)\n   217\t\n   218\t- **[47f.1] Retries cannot decide whether the scored test is complete.**\n   219\t  - The run sends every first attempt (all 36) before any retry.\n   220\t  - Completeness is judged on the first attempts: each must end published, held or refused.\n   221\t  - A retry that fails in transport, is interrupted or is never sent stays in the diagnostic record.\n   222\t  - Rehearsed: an interruption during a retry leaves all 36 scored attempts and a complete verdict. A transport failure on a retry\n   223\t    leaves the verdict complete. An interruption during a scored attempt makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. In the journal, every first\n   224\t    attempt comes before every retry.\n   225\t- **[47f.2] Every returned text survives.**\n   226\t  - The record keeps the provider's whole response, as the archive stores it, with no 20,000-character cut.\n   227\t  - A null content is shown as the model's refusal, or as \"no text returned\".\n   228\t  - Both files are rendered before anything is written, and a failed render leaves no files.\n   229\t  - Rehearsed: a refusal with null content, a 25,000-character malformed answer whose passage is named at its end, and a render that\n   230\t    fails and then succeeds.\n   231\t- **Rehearsal:** 61 of 61, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   232\t- **Mutants:** 30 of 30 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`). Two mutants are caught by the crash the defence prevents:\n   233\t  - without the interrupted branch, the summary fails on an unfinished attempt;\n   234\t  - passing a null content on, packet rendering fails.\n   235\t\n   236\t## 3h. After council round 47g (`codex-r47g.md`)\n   237\t\n   238\t- **[47g] Two journals, read on the writer's own delimiter.**\n   239\t  - Scored first attempts are written to `answers.jsonl`, and diagnostic retries to `retries.jsonl`. The run digest covers both.\n   240\t  - A damaged line in `answers.jsonl` makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. A damaged line in `retries.jsonl` is reported and marks that retry\n   241\t    interrupted, but leaves the scored test complete.\n   242\t  - Records are split on '\\n' only, the writer's delimiter. An answer may contain other Unicode line separators (U+2028, U+0085,\n   243\t    U+2029), and these are kept inside the record.\n   244\t  - Rehearsed: a torn retry record leaves the verdict complete; a torn scored record (the existing control) makes it INCOMPLETE; an\n   245\t    answer holding U+2028, U+0085 and U+2029 stays one record; the order of every first attempt before any retry is checked on the\n   246\t    provider's own call sequence.\n   247\t- **Rehearsal:** 63 of 63, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   248\t- **Mutants:** 33 of 33 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   249\t  - One mutant (splitting on any line break) is caught when a scenario guard stops the rehearsal: 36 attempts started, 35 finished.\n   250\t  - The mutant harness now counts such a stop as a catch and shows its reason.\n   251\t\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n   283\t\n   284\t## D753. The one-time v13s re-send (Alex: \"破例一次，付费重发\"), prepared before any answer exists\n   285\t\n   286\t- **The plan.** `paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned `0dc7c310…` in `paid-plan-v13s.sha256`. It holds 12 requests × 3 draws = 36 first\n   287\t  attempts. Every request's system text is the registered D751 request (`080a0012…`). The cases are unchanged: three pairs, then O,\n   288\t  S (CY2027) and E.\n   289\t- **The cap.** $0.50 in total, diagnostic retries included (D732 and D753).\n   290\t- **Authorization.** One-time, at `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/authorization.json`. The spent v13 authorization and the v13 pin\n   291\t  are unchanged. `send()` picks the pin and the authorization by the plan's format and refuses a mixed plan.\n   292\t- **Checked at $0,** with a stub gate and scratch key paths:\n   293\t  - an altered plan is refused, and so is a wrong ceiling;\n   294\t  - the pinned plan passes;\n   295\t  - a second use of the authorization is refused, and so is the spent v13 plan.\n   296\t- **Changes from council round 70** (`codex-r70.md`), made before the send. The verdict lines, the four questions and the\n   297\t  third-reader rule are unchanged.\n   298\t  1. **The card renderer** (`card_view`, `normalise`) now shows:\n   299\t     - every figure and passage the card's prose names, with the figures they rest on;\n   300\t     - a written range such as e5399–e5404 in full, with no width limit (council 70b);\n   301\t     - every passage in the card's `pushes` (council 70b: an unresolved E card had hidden 6 of the 15 passages it weighed). Figure ids inside the prose (reasons, why, basis_text) are\n   302\t     renumbered with the figures, so a prose reference points to the figure the writer meant.\n   303\t     - Checked at $0 on 20 stored v13s answers (D749–D751 and two controls): no dangling figure or passage reference, and every\n   304\t       shown value equal to the writer's.\n   305\t     - The re-check after council 70b covered every passage the answer names at card level (cites, pushes and prose, ranges\n   306\t       expanded). Missing: 0 of 20. Each unresolved card shows all 15 of its passages.\n   307\t  2. **The reader brief** is `reader-brief-v13s.md`. It is the v13 brief with Alex's two rulings, the same words for both readers and\n   308\t     the third reader:\n   309\t     - `usable` accepts an explained related figure (D747) and a \"can't tell yet\" that weighs the evidence, gives the target as\n   310\t       context and names the deciding fact (D753);\n   311\t     - `deciding_gap` is yes for a published number whose band an unsized adjustment determines, and no for a \"can't tell yet\".\n   312\t  3. **The exact file.** Readers receive the exact `packets.md` (`assemble_readings.py split-exact`; `third-exact` for the third\n   313\t     reader), with their packet ids named separately, so the sha256 the readings carry is the text they read.\n   314\t  4. **The launch.** It runs from the repository root, detached, with the log and pid outside the run folder:\n   315\t     `python3 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py send poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 0.5\n   316\t     docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.json`.\n   317\t     - All 36 scored attempts precede any diagnostic retry.\n   318\t     - A terminal transport failure on a first attempt makes the result INCOMPLETE.\n   319\t- **Re-checked after the changes:** rehearsal 19 of 19, paid mutants 33 of 33 with the control passing, cases 111 of 111, and the plan\n   320\t  pin unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D(72[5-9]|73[0-9]|74[0-9]|75[0-4])\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -100; rg -n '\"'^#|§0'\"' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D(72[5-9]|73[0-9]|74[0-9]|75[0-4])\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -100; rg -n '\"'^#|§0'\"' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\"","aggregated_output":"10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n10993:- **The questions** (after D725):\n11001:  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n11008:## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n11041:## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n11043:- **The question** (after D727): \"新判官算数的时候，要不要让它看到自己上一次的预测？… 不给看的代价：以前靠'上次结论'带着的那些老证据（这次没展示的）就丢了，只剩最近被引用过的和新到的证据。\"\n11055:## D729 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate passes (council round 46ad); the paid gate needs its harness built at $0 and Alex's ceiling\n11067:- **Not shown:** how a model uses the format (the paid gate, D725), production lifecycle, the product request builder.\n11073:## D730 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: build the paid gate's harness at $0, then ask for the ceiling\n11075:- **The question** (after D729): \"要不要现在接着搭花钱测试用的发送程序和盲审材料？搭的过程不花钱，搭好、演练、过 council 之后再问你上限（预计 36 次调用，0.2–0.4 美元）。\"\n11080:- **Decided (Alex):** the sender and the blind reading packets for D725's paid gate are built, rehearsed at $0 and reviewed by the\n11083:## D731 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid-gate harness is ready to send (council round 47h); the first attempt is scored on both arms; the ceiling is Alex's\n11085:- **What was built (D730):** `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py` (plan, send, recover, packets, verdict, replay),\n11090:- **Decided by the council (D725's lines unchanged):**\n11091:  - The first attempt is scored on both arms. D725 registers the arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about\n11110:## D732 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the paid gate's ceiling is $0.50\n11112:- **The question** (after D731): \"judging-v13 花钱那一关（36 次计分请求，按公开价格约 0.17 美元，最坏 0.39 美元；重试排在最后、只作诊断）已经过理事会，现在可以发。你给多少上限？\"\n11122:## D733 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's paid gate: STOP, every answer refused; the format's rules were never stated in the request (council round 48); repair or close is Alex's choice\n11124:- **What ran** (D732): 36 scored first attempts and 36 diagnostic retries, gpt-6-luna, $0.3677 of $0.50 (ledger: 72 attempts,\n11126:- **Registered result (D725's lines, scored as written, D680):** all 72 answers refused by `calc_check.py`, none published; the joint\n11129:- **What it measures:** not D725's question (whether one call over a family gives better numbers), only that the answer format, as\n11163:    - Only then is a re-send of the same 36 requests asked for, under a new decision with D725's lines unchanged.\n11169:## D734 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: repair judging-v13's request and checks once, then a $0 blind conformance test\n11171:- **The question** (after D733): \"判数字的新版本（一次判一组相关的数）花钱那一关没过：72 个答案全被挡在“填格式”这一步。原因是填写规则只写在检查代码里、没写进给模型的说明，而且检查代码自己也会把对的判错。这没回答“一起判会不会更准”。下一步怎么走？\"\n11176:- **Decided (Alex):** one bounded repair of judging-v13's request and checks, per council round 48 (D733).\n11180:  - A clean result goes back to Alex as a request to re-send the same 36 requests under a new decision, with D725's lines\n11185:## D735 · 2026-11-22 · Council rounds 49–50: the repair is finished to a line; at most two more review rounds, then the blind test\n11194:  - Codex answered that the six drop C8's guard against adding a segment into its total, a defect D725 named. Shrinking changes the\n11195:    design and exceeds D734.\n11196:  - Consensus: finish D734's repair to a line. One round reviews the exact wording and cases, one reviews the request the harness\n11210:## D736 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 51: the repair's wording review finds as many serious issues as round 49; Claude and Codex split on going back to Alex now\n11230:  - **Codex:** fix the round-51 issues, use the second allowed round (D735) on the sent request and checks, and return to Alex only\n11232:  - **Claude:** go back to Alex now. Round 51's evidence came after D735's consensus. Shrinking the checks is the structural rule,\n11233:    and it is his to choose, because it exceeds D734.\n11236:## D737 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: shrink judging-v13's format to the checks that stop the named defects, then a $0 blind test\n11238:- **The question** (after D736): \"判数字新版本的修补连续三轮审查都在冒新规则（填写说明将从 1 万字涨到约 2 万字，每个答案约 16 个数、每个数要同时满足几十条规则）。Codex 主张修完再审最后一轮；我主张现在改结构。下一步怎么走？\"\n11255:    D725's lines.\n11256:- **Superseded:** REPAIR-DESIGN.md v2's full restatement (D735's finish line), replaced by the small format.\n11258:## D738 · 2026-11-22 · v13s: code refuses a named defect only where the calculation's structure decides it; readers mark the five defects on every reply (council rounds 52–53)\n11260:- **Rounds 52 and 53** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r52.md`, `codex-r53.md`) reviewed the small format within D737's\n11265:- **Settled (how D737's rule is built; D737 says code refuses only for the five defects, not that code catches every instance):**\n11290:## D739 · 2026-11-22 · v13s built and rehearsed; council round 54's findings fixed; the blind test runs, and its result goes to Council B\n11325:## D740 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s blind test stops on a checker error and a reader-marked defect; council round 55 sends three reader rulings to Alex\n11346:## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n11348:- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n11361:- **How they are applied (D738):**\n11365:    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n11369:## D742 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s re-run stops on one sound answer refused by S4; council 56–56c keeps S4 and makes the request state one benchmark rule; a third $0 blind run follows\n11383:      O's rung, and D741 ruling 2 does not settle it.\n11397:- **Decided (council, under Alex's \"那你自己持续迭代\" and D741 ruling 1):**\n11408:     The stop lines are unchanged (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).\n11416:## D743 · 2026-11-22 · The third v13s blind run stops on the reader brief; the writer side is clean; council 57 asks Alex to authorize a re-reading\n11421:    - all six P-family writers recorded the Q4 pace as an estimate naming its benchmark (D742's rule);\n11449:## D744 · 2026-11-22 · The D743 re-read fixes the range rule but stops on the midpoint; one mechanism (readers lack the writer's format rules); council 58 asks Alex for one more bounded re-read under shared rule text\n11484:## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n11501:  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\n11516:- **Council round 60** (`codex-r60.md`) set the wording and the registration (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D745]):\n11524:## D746 · 2026-11-23 · The D745 targeted test fails on E's unsized cut; S splits on how far an indirect comparison can support a forecast; council 61–61b: one general question to Alex, then a $0 stored-answer re-read; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11547:       - D741 ruling 3 still requires a stated deduction or a supported bound. The threshold for \"supported\" when the support is an\n11549:    2. **Writers size a risk without evidence.** 3 of 4 E replies across two runs carry a disputed cut or share, and D745's sentence\n11552:    - Claude withdrew two reasons for the lean. D725 does not promise that code catches every invented figure. AGENTS §8's \"no data to\n11565:      open in practice. A clean re-read does not turn D745 into a pass.\n11573:## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n11575:- **The question** (after D746): \"资料没直接给出题目问的那个数，只能拿一个相关的数字来比。比如问四大云厂商今年的数据中心开支能不能过 7000 亿，资料只说“这四家 AI 基础设施开支超过 7300 亿”。这种比较能说明结果更可能落在线的某一边，但另一边也还有可能。这时系统可以发布预测吗，还是要等资料能直接算出落在哪边？\"\n11586:  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n11588:  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n11589:- **Next (D746).** The ruling's words go into the shared reader definitions (`blind_rules.py`). Then one $0 blinded re-read of nine\n11592:## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11598:    - The code did not catch it. The figure is linked only to the 98% share, and the floor is claimed in prose. D738 leaves that\n11618:      On U02, one side accepted the band and the other required the writer's stated route. D747 already rejects U02's route. No\n11624:  - **The recommendation.** Ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair despite the three disclosed splits. D746 made the repair\n11641:## D749 · 2026-11-23 · Alex authorizes the E writer repair and its $0 writer test\n11643:- **The question** (after D748): \"下一步怎么走？\"\n11653:  blind writer test on E, S and P-v8, with the saved U05 (invented cut) and U02 (impossible floor) as reader controls, under D748's\n11656:## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n11681:  is registered (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D750]) and built by `blind6.py`. Council round 66 reviews it before any send.\n11683:## D751 · 2026-11-23 · D750 fails on E's bracket midpoint; council 67–68 (under D439): one structural line-9 change, a paper check first, then one last writer test with an exit rule back to Alex\n11685:- **The D750 result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md`): FAIL on one settled line.\n11699:  - Claude's lean was to stop the $0 loop and ask Alex to waive D749's clean-pass condition for the paid re-send.\n11704:- **Council round 68** (`codex-r68.md`) verified Claude's paper check (`PAPER-CHECK-D751.md`) row by row:\n11710:  It replaced \"across the plausible readings\", which was stricter than D747, with: \"When other evidence bears on the forecast, weigh\n11716:  - the test registered (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D751]) and built by `blind7.py`: D750's design and tally, with the exit rule.\n11718:  spending. Council 67 would uphold it under D741 ruling 2's \"an outside figure for the member's own quantity\". The reader definition\n11721:## D752 · 2026-11-23 · D751 fails, so the wording loop ends under its exit rule; council 69–69b: two questions to Alex (the E-type publication default, agreed; the paid re-send, split)\n11723:- **The D751 result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md`): FAIL on one settled line.\n11735:  - P-v8 was supported in every run, and the controls were caught 6 of 6 since D749. S is mixed.\n11736:  - Only the paid gate compares joint against reconciled separate pairs, D725's hypothesis. No free test can answer it.\n11737:- **The exit rule fired** (council 67, registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D751]). The wording loop ends, and the publication choice\n11742:    change, because line 9 already states it and Alex endorsed it (D745, D749). The alternative, the target's band by default, would\n11745:    - Codex recommends keeping the paid re-send on hold, because Alex made a clean free pass the condition and D751 failed.\n11754:## D753 · 2026-11-23 · Alex chooses \"can't tell yet\" as the E-type default and a one-time paid exception\n11756:- **The questions** (after D752):\n11771:  2. A one-time exception to D749's clean-pass condition: the paid re-send of the 36 requests, rebuilt in v13s with the D751 request,\n11772:     under D725's lines and the paid gate's reading rule (`PAID-GATE.md` §4), with a total cap of $0.50 including diagnostic\n11775:## D754 · 2026-11-23 · The one-time v13s paid re-send is prepared, reviewed in council 70–70c, and sent under Alex's D753\n11777:- **Prepared at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md`, the last section \"D753\"):\n11778:  - the v13s plan `paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned `0dc7c310…`: 12 requests × 3 draws, the D751 request;\n11781:  prose figure references pointing to the wrong figure after renumbering. It also asked for Alex's D747 and D753 rulings in the reader\n1:# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n12:## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n25:## 1. Goal (end to end)\n31:## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n57:## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n67:| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n70:## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n93:## 5. What to do\n120:## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n168:## 7. Process (no drift)\n179:## 8. Steps and where we are\n193:## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
