{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 && python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor name in ('answers.jsonl','retries.jsonl','plan.json','results.json','reading/codex.json','reading/claude.json','reading/third.json','reading/readings.json','verdict.json','ledger.json'):\n s=open(name).readlines()\n x=json.loads(s[0] if name.endswith('jsonl') else ''.join(s))\n print(name,len(s), {k:(type(v).__name__,len(v) if isinstance(v,(list,dict,str)) else v) for k,v in x.items()} if isinstance(x,dict) else (len(x),str(x[0])[:400]))\n if name in ('plan.json','results.json','reading/readings.json'): \n  for k,v in x.items():\n   if isinstance(v,list) and v: print(k,str(list(v[0]) if isinstance(v[0],dict) else v[0])[:1800])\n if name=='verdict.json':print(''.join(s))\nPY\nrg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' packets.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 && python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor name in ('answers.jsonl','retries.jsonl','plan.json','results.json','reading/codex.json','reading/claude.json','reading/third.json','reading/readings.json','verdict.json','ledger.json'):\n s=open(name).readlines()\n x=json.loads(s[0] if name.endswith('jsonl') else ''.join(s))\n print(name,len(s), {k:(type(v).__name__,len(v) if isinstance(v,(list,dict,str)) else v) for k,v in x.items()} if isinstance(x,dict) else (len(x),str(x[0])[:400]))\n if name in ('plan.json','results.json','reading/readings.json'): \n  for k,v in x.items():\n   if isinstance(v,list) and v: print(k,str(list(v[0]) if isinstance(v[0],dict) else v[0])[:1800])\n if name=='verdict.json':print(''.join(s))\nPY\nrg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' packets.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"zsh:1: can't create temp file for here document: operation not permitted\n3:## P01\n4:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?\n56:## P02\n57:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\n122:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n190:## P03\n191:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?\n242:## P04\n243:### Card K1: How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n282:## P05\n283:### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n334:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n381:## P06\n382:### Card K1: How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n408:## P07\n409:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n448:### Card K2: What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\n484:## P08\n485:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n558:### Card K2: What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\n626:## P09\n627:### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n664:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n709:## P10\n710:### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n755:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n808:## P11\n809:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n884:### Card K2: What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\n955:## P12\n956:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\n1003:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1068:## P13\n1069:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n1129:### Card K2: What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\n1179:## P14\n1180:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n1234:### Card K2: What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\n1293:## P15\n1294:### Card K1: How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\n1354:## P16\n1355:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?\n1408:## P17\n1409:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\n1477:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1562:## P18\n1563:### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1603:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1652:## P19\n1653:### Card K1: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n1687:## P20\n1688:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\n1742:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1793:## P21\n1794:### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1833:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1880:## P22\n1881:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\n1937:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n1988:## P23\n1989:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\n2033:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n2120:## P24\n2121:### Card K1: How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n2173:### Card K2: How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\n2234:## P25\n2235:### Card K1: What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\n2308:### Card K2: What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\n2356:## P26\n2357:### Card K1: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n2409:## P27\n2410:### Card K1: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10957,11010p;11089,11109p;11240,11289p;11348,11369p;11573,11593p;11721,11797p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '247,282p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10957,11010p;11089,11109p;11240,11289p;11348,11369p;11573,11593p;11721,11797p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '247,282p'\"","aggregated_output":"## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n- **Diagnosis:**\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n     figures.\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n- **Measured:**\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n    reference);\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n  - extraction unchanged;\n  - families declared for the test.\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n- **The questions** (after D725):\n  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n    ceiling.\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\n\n## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n\n- **Design:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md`, v1 to v9. Council rounds 46 to 46e reached READY FOR THE $0 GATE on v5.\n  with a rehearsal case and a mutant; round 47h answered \"READY TO SEND (once Alex names the ceiling)\".\n- **Decided by the council (D725's lines unchanged):**\n  - The first attempt is scored on both arms. D725 registers the arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about\n    retries. A joint retry can repair a cross-card conflict that the separate arm sees only after both calls end, so scoring the\n    final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have. Retries are sent after every first\n    attempt and read for diagnosis only (`attempts.md`, `retries.jsonl`).\n  - The readers' packets hold only what their four questions need, per card the scored answer's passages, figures, recomputed\n    outcome, assumptions and card. No attempt history, code decision or check code (a cross-member code would reveal the arm).\n  - The text the readers receive commits to the packet-to-unit mapping: a salted key's sha256 is its first line. The verdict renders\n    every packet again from the run and refuses any mismatch.\n  - The separate arm's two answers are reconciled one to one: a declared shared forecast is unified only when each call holds exactly\n    one, with the same value, bounds and unit.\n  - Completeness is judged on the scored attempts. The readings are sealed into the run, the verdict is written once, and `replay`\n    must reproduce it.\n- **Checks:** rehearsal 63 of 63 (three runs); mutants 33 of 33 caught, the control passes; the $0 gate unchanged (87 of 87, gate run 27).\n- **Cost, at `hivemind.model.PRICES` (gpt-6-luna $0.10 input, $0.50 output per million tokens; tokens estimated as characters / 4):**\n  - the 36 first attempts are about $0.17 at 4,000 output tokens each, and at most $0.39 if every answer used its 16,000-token cap;\n  - the budget transport reserves at most $0.039 for one request before sending;\n  - so $0.50 covers every scored attempt. Retries come last, and a ceiling stop among them leaves the scored test complete.\n- **Next:** Alex names the ceiling (proposed $0.50). Nothing has been sent.\n\n  - 砍成小格式再盲测 (recommended): keep only the checks that stop five defects (a number misread, wrong arithmetic, a part\n    above its whole or added into it, two forecasts of one quarter, an own estimate passed off as the market's); the other rules\n    become assumptions shown to readers; council, then the $0 blind test, then a request for the paid re-send;\n  - 按原计划再修一轮 (Codex's position);\n  - 关掉这条线.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22), the recommended option (\"…成小格式再盲测 (推荐)\").\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - The judging-v13 format shrinks. Code refuses an answer only for the five defects above and for broken structure (links that do\n    not resolve, a cycle, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome not of the question's quantity, a rung that does not hold the\n    outcome).\n  - Each such rule is written in one or two sentences beside its field. Every other rule of DESIGN.md's checks becomes an assumption\n    recorded and shown to the readers, never a refusal.\n  - The council reviews within that scope. A counterexample that lets none of the five defects through is a reader's matter, not a\n    finding.\n  - Then the $0 blind test (REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5, with round 51's reader fix). A clean result returns to Alex for the paid re-send under\n    D725's lines.\n- **Superseded:** REPAIR-DESIGN.md v2's full restatement (D735's finish line), replaced by the small format.\n\n## D738 · 2026-11-22 · v13s: code refuses a named defect only where the calculation's structure decides it; readers mark the five defects on every reply (council rounds 52–53)\n\n- **Rounds 52 and 53** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r52.md`, `codex-r53.md`) reviewed the small format within D737's\n  scope. Each closing rule written for an indirect form of a named defect produced new counterexamples in both directions:\n  - \"uses the part\" lineage refuses a correct sum of two Data Center quarters, each computed as a share of company revenue;\n  - \"one figure per quantity\" refuses two outside estimates averaged into one starting point;\n  - multiplying by 1, relabelling a basis, or routing through an estimate's judgement still passes.\n- **Settled (how D737's rule is built; D737 says code refuses only for the five defects, not that code catches every instance):**\n  - Code refuses a named defect where the calculation's own structure decides it without reading intent:\n    - **S8:** a sum whose inputs include the part's quantity and the whole's quantity themselves.\n    - **S4:** two figures with basis forecast for one quantity and period, or a figure of a listed shared quantity used by an outcome\n      on a path that bypasses its forecast figure.\n    - **S3:** a part above its whole, compared with paired ends when the part is computed from the whole and lowest against highest\n      otherwise, on recomputed values. A share takes 0 to 100 percent.\n    - **S5:** an estimate or forecast at or beneath the marked reference.\n    - **S1, S2, S6, S7** as written.\n  - Indirect forms (a multiplier of one, a relabelled basis, an estimate's judgement) are recorded for readers. They are never\n    refused.\n  - **The readers** in the blind test and the gate mark the five defects on every reply. In the blind test, an accepted reply with\n    a reader-marked defect is a stop, so whether real writers use these forms is measured, not argued.\n  - **Round 53's false refusals and test conflicts are fixed in the design:**\n    - DC Q3 + Q4;\n    - averaged outside inputs;\n    - cycles through `rests_on`;\n    - a figure used twice taking one value in range arithmetic;\n    - the \"to\", \"+/-\" and \"±\" spellings;\n    - one-source \"±\";\n    - the separate arm carrying the part-of relation for S8;\n    - readers given the whole reply and every shown passage.\n- **Next:** build `calc_small.py`, the v13s schema, header and plan, and the A1–A4 cases and mutants. Council round 54 reviews the code\n  and the end-to-end rehearsal. Then comes the blind test.\n\n- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n- **How they are applied (D738):**\n  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n  - Then three steps:\n    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n\n## D742 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s re-run stops on one sound answer refused by S4; council 56–56c keeps S4 and makes the request state one benchmark rule; a third $0 blind run follows\n## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n\n- **The question** (after D746): \"资料没直接给出题目问的那个数，只能拿一个相关的数字来比。比如问四大云厂商今年的数据中心开支能不能过 7000 亿，资料只说“这四家 AI 基础设施开支超过 7300 亿”。这种比较能说明结果更可能落在线的某一边，但另一边也还有可能。这时系统可以发布预测吗，还是要等资料能直接算出落在哪边？\"\n  - Options:\n    - \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\": the answer must explain why the comparison applies to the companies, the year and the quantity\n      asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side is more likely; an answer that cannot explain it is not supported;\n    - \"先说“还判断不了”\";\n    - \"先停在这里\".\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex).** When the passages do not give the asked quantity, a forecast may rest on a related figure. It is supported\n  only when the answer explains two things: why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked; and why,\n  under the answer's own stated assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely. An answer that cannot explain this is not\n  supported.\n  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n    bound.\n  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n- **Next (D746).** The ruling's words go into the shared reader definitions (`blind_rules.py`). Then one $0 blinded re-read of nine\n  stored answers, registered with its expected readings and reviewed by the council before any packet is read.\n\n## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n\n## D752 · 2026-11-23 · D751 fails, so the wording loop ends under its exit rule; council 69–69b: two questions to Alex (the E-type publication default, agreed; the paid re-send, split)\n\n- **The D751 result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND7-RESULT.md`): FAIL on one settled line.\n  - X01, E Claude, $37B: the 85% growth was an interpolation between the market pace and \"more than double\"; no passage sizes a\n    shortfall.\n  - Passed:\n    - E Codex: a justified \"can't tell\", for the third run in a row;\n    - S Codex: supported;\n    - both P-v8 forecasts: supported;\n    - both controls: caught.\n  - Split: S Claude's $20B deduction.\n- **The record across the five runs** (`BLIND7-RESULT.md` §2):\n  - The Codex writer invented cuts twice, then gave three justified \"can't tell\" answers on E, each accepted by both families.\n  - The Claude writer's five E forecasts never earned settled support (four settled no, one split).\n  - P-v8 was supported in every run, and the controls were caught 6 of 6 since D749. S is mixed.\n  - Only the paid gate compares joint against reconciled separate pairs, D725's hypothesis. No free test can answer it.\n- **The exit rule fired** (council 67, registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D751]). The wording loop ends, and the publication choice\n  for E-type cases returns to Alex.\n- **Council round 69** (`codex-r69.md`) and **69b** (`codex-r69b.md`):\n  - **Agreed, question 1.** When a reaffirmed target sits near a band line and, after weighing it with the other evidence, neither\n    band is more likely, the recommended default is \"can't tell yet\", naming the fact that would decide it. It needs no request\n    change, because line 9 already states it and Alex endorsed it (D745, D749). The alternative, the target's band by default, would\n    be a new publication policy.\n  - **Split, question 2.**\n    - Codex recommends keeping the paid re-send on hold, because Alex made a clean free pass the condition and D751 failed.\n    - Claude recommends a one-time exception, because only the paid run measures luna and the joint-against-separate comparison,\n      within Alex's own $0.50 cap. Under the gate's lines, an E-type failure by luna would show as STOP rather than hide.\n    - Both agree the exception must be presented with its case. The 36 scored requests and any diagnostic retries share the $0.50\n      cap, and a pass earns design work only.\n  - **Claude's overstatement, corrected.** \"The Claude writer failed five times\" became \"none of five forecasts earned settled\n    support; one split\".\n- **Pending:** Alex's answers to the two questions. Under D439 nothing paid is started.\n\n## D753 · 2026-11-23 · Alex chooses \"can't tell yet\" as the E-type default and a one-time paid exception\n\n- **The questions** (after D752):\n  1. \"公司重申一个目标，正好落在两个预测档之间的那条线附近（比如 Vera CPU 明年“超过翻倍”，正好压在 400 亿线上）。把目标和其他证据都权衡过，还是说不出哪一档更可能。这时系统应该给读者看什么？\" Options:\n     - \"显示“暂时判断不了” (推荐)\": the target as context, \"can't tell yet\", and the missing fact named; the council agreed; no\n       request change;\n     - \"按公司目标所在的档\".\n  2. \"最后一次不花钱的写手测试里，有一份 E 题预测被两家都判了没依据，没达到你定的“0 元测试干净通过才付费”。理事会在这一题上意见不一：Codex 主张先不付费，我主张破例一次。你选哪个？\" Options:\n     - \"先不付费，停在这里\" (Codex);\n     - \"破例一次，付费重发\" (Claude): 36 requests to luna, ≤ $0.50 including retries; a pass earns design work only, and an E-type\n       forced number stops the run;\n     - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23): \"显示“暂时判断不了” (推荐)\"; \"破例一次，付费重发\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  1. When a reaffirmed target sits near a band line and, after weighing it with the other evidence, neither band is more likely, the\n     system shows \"can't tell yet\" with the target as context and names the deciding fact. The request already states it (line 9);\n     nothing changes.\n  2. A one-time exception to D749's clean-pass condition: the paid re-send of the 36 requests, rebuilt in v13s with the D751 request,\n     under D725's lines and the paid gate's reading rule (`PAID-GATE.md` §4), with a total cap of $0.50 including diagnostic\n     retries. It is prepared at $0 and reviewed by the council before the send.\n\n## D754 · 2026-11-23 · The one-time v13s paid re-send is prepared, reviewed in council 70–70c, and sent under Alex's D753\n\n- **Prepared at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md`, the last section \"D753\"):\n  - the v13s plan `paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned `0dc7c310…`: 12 requests × 3 draws, the D751 request;\n  - a separate one-time authorization path and pin selection in `send()`, checked with a stub gate and scratch keys.\n- **Council round 70** (`codex-r70.md`) found that the paid card renderer would show readers a distorted answer: lost passages, and\n  prose figure references pointing to the wrong figure after renumbering. It also asked for Alex's D747 and D753 rulings in the reader\n  text, and for the exact packets file to reach the readers.\n  - Fixed: `card_view`, `normalise`, `reader-brief-v13s.md`, and `assemble_readings.py split-exact` / `third-exact`.\n- **Round 70b** blocked the send twice over: `pushes[]` passages were still hidden (6 of 15 on an unresolved E card), and the range\n  expansion had a width limit I had added.\n  - Both were fixed. The re-check covered every passage named at card level: missing 0 of 20 stored answers, every prose reference\n    resolving, every value the writer's.\n- **Round 70c:** \"send\".\n  - It checked all 20 cards and 208 figures, the plan pin byte for byte, and that the authorization and run folder were absent.\n- **Re-checked:** rehearsal 19 of 19, paid mutants 33 of 33 with the control passing, cases 111 of 111.\n- **Sent** (2026-11-23):\n  - `python3 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py send poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 0.5 …/paid-plan-v13s.json`,\n    detached;\n  - log `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23.log`, pid `poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23.pid`;\n  - authorization written at `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/authorization.json` (ceiling 0.5, plan `0dc7c310…`).\n- **Next:** when it finishes, `packets` (key in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/`); two blind readers per packet on the exact file;\n  a third Codex reader on disagreements; `assemble`; one `verdict`. Then read every trace, then council B.\n   247\t- **Rehearsal:** 63 of 63, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   248\t- **Mutants:** 33 of 33 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   249\t  - One mutant (splitting on any line break) is caught when a scenario guard stops the rehearsal: 36 attempts started, 35 finished.\n   250\t  - The mutant harness now counts such a stop as a catch and shows its reason.\n   251\t\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
