{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'ls -d /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/python3 /Users/lchingen/.pyenv/versions/*/bin/python3(N) /Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/*/bin/python3(N); cd poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 && for f in plan.json results.json reading/{readings,claude,codex,third}.json verdict.json; do wc -l \"$f\"; head -c 999 \"$f\"; echo; done'","aggregated_output":"/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.11-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.11.15-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.12-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.12.13-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.13-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.local/share/uv/python/cpython-3.13.1-macos-aarch64-none/bin/python3\n/Users/lchingen/.pyenv/versions/3.10.10/bin/python3\n       0 plan.json\n[{\"unit\": \"pair-old-1\", \"arm\": \"joint\", \"draw_store\": \"old-1\", \"members\": [\"v4\", \"v8\"], \"format\": \"v13s\", \"system\": \"You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\\n\\n- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\\n- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or g\n   40521 results.json\n{\n \"finals\": {\n  \"pair-old-1|joint|1\": {\n   \"status\": \"answered\",\n   \"data\": {\n    \"figures\": [\n     {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"what\": {\n       \"population\": \"NVIDIA\",\n       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n       \"scope\": \"company\",\n       \"period\": \"FY2027 Q1\"\n      },\n      \"kind\": \"source\",\n      \"basis\": \"reported\",\n      \"value\": 81.62,\n      \"low\": null,\n      \"high\": null,\n      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e111\",\n      \"quote_number\": \"$81.62 billion\",\n      \"qualifier\": \"none\",\n      \"inputs\": null,\n      \"operation\": null,\n      \"basis_text\": null,\n      \"rests_on\": null,\n      \"outcome_for\": [],\n      \"reference_for\": []\n     },\n     {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"what\": {\n       \"population\": \"NVIDIA\",\n       \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n       \"scope\": \"company\",\n       \"period\": \"FY2027 Q2\"\n      },\n      \"kind\": \"source\",\n      \"basis\": \"reported\",\n      \"value\": 96.2,\n      \"low\": null,\n      \"high\": null,\n      \"unit\": \"USD bn\",\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e2649\",\n      \"quote_numbe\n    1836 reading/readings.json\n{\n \"packets_sha256\": \"078038c12132199937070032e8b24f0c0ffd279f96d4d6aa46a3d42c4ceb4912\",\n \"packets\": {\n  \"P01\": {\n   \"K1\": {\n    \"A\": {\n     \"usable\": {\n      \"answer\": \"yes\",\n      \"ground\": \"The Vera-specific outlook in e4691 and e4856 supports a forecast near $40 billion, while Anthropic is still evaluating Vera in e5044, giving K1 little basis to expect $50 billion.\"\n     },\n     \"contradiction\": {\n      \"answer\": \"no\",\n      \"ground\": \"K1 is the only card in P01.\"\n     },\n     \"internal_reference\": {\n      \"answer\": \"no\",\n      \"ground\": \"K1 attributes the $40 billion benchmark to management and labels F4's $43 billion as its own forecast.\"\n     },\n     \"deciding_gap\": {\n      \"answer\": \"no\",\n      \"ground\": \"F4's estimated $3 billion increase leaves the forecast in the same $40 billion to under $50 billion band as F3.\"\n     }\n    },\n    \"B\": {\n     \"usable\": {\n      \"answer\": \"yes\",\n      \"ground\": \"F3 ($40bn) follows from the $20bn FY2027 base and the more-than-double outlook i\n     865 reading/claude.json\n{\n \"P01\": {\n  \"K1\": {\n   \"usable\": {\n    \"answer\": \"yes\",\n    \"ground\": \"F3 ($40bn) follows from the $20bn FY2027 base and the more-than-double outlook in e3660, and e4856 ties that outlook to Vera CPU, so the floor sits at rung 2's lower edge. K1 explains why its $43bn estimate F4 stays below $50bn: no sized orders, e5044 is only an evaluation, and e5399-e5404 show competitive risk.\"\n   },\n   \"contradiction\": {\n    \"answer\": \"no\",\n    \"ground\": \"P01 holds only one card, K1.\"\n   },\n   \"internal_reference\": {\n    \"answer\": \"no\",\n    \"ground\": \"K1's reference is F3, which is computed from management's guidance in e3660. K1's own estimate F4 is labelled as its forecast, not as the market's expectation.\"\n   },\n   \"deciding_gap\": {\n    \"answer\": \"no\",\n    \"ground\": \"The rung 2 floor comes from the sized guidance F1 x F2 (e3660). e4856 and e4691 resolve the CPU-to-Vera scope. Even an exact doubling gives $40bn, which is still rung 2, so no unsized adjustment decides the band.\"\n   }\n  }\n },\n\n     865 reading/codex.json\n{\n \"P01\": {\n  \"K1\": {\n   \"usable\": {\n    \"answer\": \"yes\",\n    \"ground\": \"The Vera-specific outlook in e4691 and e4856 supports a forecast near $40 billion, while Anthropic is still evaluating Vera in e5044, giving K1 little basis to expect $50 billion.\"\n   },\n   \"contradiction\": {\n    \"answer\": \"no\",\n    \"ground\": \"K1 is the only card in P01.\"\n   },\n   \"internal_