ers': ['refused', 'refused']}, 'pair-old-1|3': {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': ['refused', 'refused']}, 'pair-old-2|1': {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': ['refused', 'publish']}, 'pair-old-2|2': {'decision': 'refused', 'errors': [['S4', 'NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3: 2 forecasts (v14.F7, v9.F3); compute it once and use that figure'], ['S4', 'NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q4: 2 forecasts (v14.F9, v9.F8); compute it once and use that figure'], ['S4', 'v14: uses NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 but the calculation has 2 forecast figures for it'], ['S4', 'v9: uses NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3 but the calculation has 2 forecast figures for it'], ['S4', 'v14: uses NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q4 but the calculation has 2 forecast figures for it'], ['S4', 'v9: uses NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q4 but the calculation has 2 forecast figures for it']], 'published': {'v14': [426.365, 426.365, None], 'v9': [377.786, 377.786, None]}, 'calc': {'figures': [{'id': 'v14.F1', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q1'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'reported', 'value': 81.6, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$81.6 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'evidence': 'e238'}, {'id': 'v14.F2', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q2'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'reported', 'value': 96.2, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$96.2 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'evidence': 'e2497'}, {'id': 'v14.F3', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 H1'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'reported', 'value': 177.8, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v14.F1', 'v14.F2'], 'operation': 'sum'}, {'id': 'v14.F4', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'guidance', 'low': 105.84, 'high': 110.16, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 'qualifier': 'none', 'evidence': 'e2499'}, {'id': 'v14.F5', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'third_party', 'low': 113, 'high': 114, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$113 billion to $114 billion', 'qualifier': 'around', 'evidence': 'e4761'}, {'id': 'v14.F6', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'third_party', 'value': 3.1, 'unit': '%', 'quote_number': '3.1%', 'qualifier': 'none', 'evidence': 'e4762'}, {'id': 'v14.F7', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 113.5, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'basis_text': \"I estimate Q3 revenue at the midpoint of the specific $113–$114 billion outside forecast. That is above the company's guidance range, but is supported by the reported pattern of beating the high end of guidance and the reported recent average overshoot.\", 'rests_on': ['v14.F4', 'v14.F5', 'v14.F6', 'e4762']}, {'id': 'v14.F8', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue growth', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 19, 'unit': '%', 'basis_text': 'My estimate is 19% sequential revenue growth in Q4. It assumes the stated Q4 hyperscale reacceleration and Vera Rubin supply build add to the Q3 run-rate, while the disclosed supply, memory, power, and data-center constraints prevent taking the much higher customer-demand indications as realized revenue.', 'rests_on': ['v14.F7', 'e3222', 'e4052', 'e4769', 'e2572', 'e2951']}, {'id': 'v14.F9', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 135.065, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v14.F7', 'v14.F8'], 'operation': 'apply_growth'}, {'id': 'v14.F10', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'consensus', 'value': 411, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$411 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'evidence': 'e4097'}, {'id': 'v14.F11', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 426.365, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v14.F3', 'v14.F7', 'v14.F9'], 'operation': 'sum'}, {'id': 'v9.F1', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 H1'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'reported', 'value': 164, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$164 billion', 'evidence': 'e4995'}, {'id': 'v9.F2', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'guidance', 'low': 105.84, 'high': 110.16, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 'evidence': 'e2499'}, {'id': 'v9.F3', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 108, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'basis_text': \"I use the midpoint of NVIDIA's Q3 guidance as the most likely company-revenue outcome for the quarter.\", 'rests_on': ['v9.F2']}, {'id': 'v9.F4', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'Data Center share of company revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q2'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'third_party', 'value': 92.5, 'unit': '%', 'quote_number': '92.5%', 'evidence': 'e3216'}, {'id': 'v9.F5', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'Data Center share of company revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 92.5, 'unit': '%', 'basis_text': 'I hold the Data Center mix at the latest reported 92.5% for Q3. The mix had risen quarter by quarter, but the evidence does not quantify a further increase for this quarter.', 'rests_on': ['v9.F4', 'e3216']}, {'id': 'v9.F6', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 99.9, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v9.F3', 'v9.F5'], 'operation': 'share'}, {'id': 'v9.F7', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'sequential revenue growth', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 14, 'unit': '%', 'basis_text': \"My estimate is 14% sequential growth in Q4: modestly faster than the 12% sequential pace implied by Q3 guidance, reflecting NVIDIA's stated expectation that hyperscale growth reaccelerates as Vera Rubin supply builds. I do not assume unconstrained demand converts fully to sales because supply remains constrained.\", 'rests_on': ['v9.F2', 'e3222', 'e4052', 'e2572', 'e4769']}, {'id': 'v9.F8', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 123.12, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v9.F3', 'v9.F7'], 'operation': 'apply_growth'}, {'id': 'v9.F9', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'Data Center share of company revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 92.5, 'unit': '%', 'basis_text': 'I keep Q4 Data Center mix at the Q2 level of 92.5%. The evidence indicates a consistently high and rising mix, but gives no Q4 mix target; holding the latest mix avoids assuming further gains.', 'rests_on': ['v9.F4', 'e3216']}, {'id': 'v9.F10', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 113.886, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v9.F8', 'v9.F9'], 'operation': 'share'}, {'id': 'v9.F11', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'kind': 'computed', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 377.786, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'inputs': ['v9.F1', 'v9.F6', 'v9.F10'], 'operation': 'sum'}, {'id': 'v9.F12', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'third_party', 'value': 300, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'quote_number': '$300 billion', 'qualifier': 'over', 'evidence': 'e2115'}], 'answers': [{'view_id': 'v14', 'shape': 'forecast', 'rung': 2, 'reasons': 'The market reference is $411 billion, which sits in rung 2. Building the year from reported first-half revenue, a Q3 estimate above guidance, and an estimated Q4 sequential increase gives a forecast of $426.365 billion, also rung 2. The evidence as a whole favors that band: the reported quarter-on-quarter growth and Q3 guidance imply continued expansion, and management expects hyperscale growth to reaccelerate as Vera Rubin supply builds. Against an outcome below rung 2, the evidence includes strong customer demand and the improving run-rate; against rung 1, supply and infrastructure constraints argue against assuming a very sharp Q4 step-up. The customer-demand indications are not themselves shipments or recognized revenue, so I discount them rather than extrapolate them in full.', 'cites': ['e238', 'e2497', 'e2499', 'e4761', 'e4762', 'e2572', 'e2951', 'e3222', 'e4052', 'e4769', 'e4097', 'e4511', 'e4512'], 'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v10', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v5', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_last'}], 'outcome': 'v14.F11', 'reference': {'figure': 'v14.F10'}}, {'view_id': 'v9', 'shape': 'forecast', 'rung': 3, 'reasons': \"The direct outside reference is Morningstar's FY2027 Data Center estimate of well over $300 billion, which places its stated lower threshold at rung 4; it is not a precise consensus point or an upper bound. The evidence-based forecast is about $378 billion, rung 3. NVIDIA reported $164 billion in Data Center revenue in H1. I forecast Q3 company revenue at the $108 billion guidance midpoint and apply the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, giving about $100 billion for Q3. For Q4, I estimate 14% sequential company-revenue growth—somewhat above the Q3-guidance-implied 12% pace because management expects hyperscale growth to reaccelerate as Vera Rubin supply builds—while keeping Data Center mix at 92.5%. These figures yield about $114 billion of Q4 Data Center revenue and about $378 billion for FY2027. The central estimate is well above $350 billion, but below $400 billion. A result below $350 billion would require Q4 Data Center revenue below about $86 billion after the first three quarters' $264 billion, inconsistent with the stated Q4 acceleration being the more likely path. Exceeding $400 billion would require more than about $136 billion in Q4, roughly 36% above the modeled Q3 Data Center revenue in one quarter. That is possible given strong demand and a product ramp, but supply constraints and the absence of a quantified Q4 ramp make it less likely than the $350–$400 billion band.\", 'cites': ['e4995', 'e2499', 'e3216', 'e3222', 'e4052', 'e2572', 'e4769', 'e2115', 'e2541', 'e2567'], 'pushes': [{'evidence_id': 'e3222', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e4052', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'evidence_id': 'e2572', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e4769', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'evidence_id': 'e2541', 'push': 'toward_last'}], 'theme_pushes': [{'view_id': 'v10', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v19', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v26', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v27', 'push': 'none'}], 'outcome': 'v9.F11', 'reference': {'figure': 'v9.F12'}}], 'unified': []}}, 'pair-old-2|3': {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': ['refused', 'refused']}, 'pair-old-3|1': {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': ['refused', 'publish']}, 'pair-old-3|2': {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': ['refused', 'refused']}, 'pair-old-3|3': {'decision': 'not reconciled', 'members': ['refused', 'refused']}}Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 20, in <module>\nKeyError: 'cards'\n\nPLAN single O [Family] members:\nThesis v29 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA's committed equity investments in ecosystem partners\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Commitments are below $25 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Commitments are at least $25 billion and below $50 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Commitments are at least $50 billion and below $75 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: Commitments are at least $75 billion and below $100 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: Commitments are at least $100 billion.\n\nRelations: none.\nShared quantities, one forecast figure each; on every arithmetic path from an outcome, through rates and multiples too, the first figure of that quantity reached is its forecast: none.\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), in USD bn, to be used exactly: v29 = NVIDIA | equity investment commitments | company | end of FY2027 (the balance at the end of FY2027, as the FY2027 annual report publishes it).\n\n[Evidence in view for the family, 35 items]\n- e1732 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:d024d71d75661d369798d307 2026-08-12] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said NVIDIA had committed to provide $70 billion in equity investments to ecosystem partners; the period covered was not specified.\n    Quote: Nvidia has committed to directly providing $70 billion in equity investments into ecosystem partners, per new research from Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya.\n- e1919 [rumour; Yahoo Finance; original source The Information 2026-08-07; from gnews:e2a48863c597e02d402f1551 2026-08-16] The Information reported on August 7, 2026, that NVIDIA planned to invest up to $3 billion in Lancium: an initial $2 billion for about 20% equity, plus up to $1 billion tied mainly to securing additional grid interconnections.\n    Quote: According to a report from The Information, published on August 7, NVIDIA will spend up to $3 billion in Lancium, a power infrastructure developer and the firm behind the Stargate data center project in Abilene, Texas. The deal is structured in two parts: an\n{'id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Short and unique, such as F1; never a passage id.'}, 'what': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'population': {'type': 'string'}, 'measure': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The quantity, such as revenue or capital expenditure; never its basis.'}, 'scope': {'type': 'string'}, 'period': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'For example FY2027, FY2027 Q3, FY2027 H1, FY2027 Q1-Q3, CY2026, end of FY2027.'}}, 'required': ['population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period'], 'additionalProperties': False, 'description': 'What the number measures. Where the request lists keys (outcome keys, shared quantities), copy them exactly.'}, 'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['source', 'computed', 'estimate'], 'description': \"source: a number written in a shown passage's quote; computed: one operation on other figures; estimate: your judgement, with its assumption in basis_text.\"}, 'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['reported', 'guidance', 'consensus', 'third_party', 'forecast'], 'description': \"reported: an actual; guidance: the company's outlook; consensus: analysts' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family's own forecast, on a computed or estimate figure only.\"}, 'value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number', 'description': 'A point. Give value, or low and high, never both.'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'low': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number', 'description': 'A range, low at most high, with value null.'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'high': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number', 'description': 'A range, low at most high, with value null.'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'unit': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['USD bn', '%', 'x'], 'description': 'USD bn: money in billions of US dollars ($1.2 trillion = 1200; $500 million = 0.5). %: a percentage as its number (7.5% = 7.5). x: a multiple (double = 2).'}, 'evidence_id': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string', 'enum': ['e1732', 'e1919', 'e1957', 'e1970', 'e1989', 'e2080', 'e2207', 'e2280', 'e2305', 'e2404', 'e2620', 'e2643', 'e2687', 'e2889', 'e3455', 'e3474', 'e3558', 'e3880', 'e3917', 'e3934', 'e4053', 'e4486', 'e4487', 'e4648', 'e4668', 'e4669', 'e4729', 'e4829', 'e4955', 'e4956', 'e5011', 'e5012', 'e5014', 'e5017', 'e5021'], 'description': 'Source only: the passage whose quote holds the number.'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'quote_number': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string', 'description': \"Source only: a complete number exactly as the quote writes it, never a piece of a longer number, range or 'plus or minus' expression, with its currency and scale or its percent sign, and nothing else: '$4.5 billion', 'US$300 million', '$2.1bn', '40%', '-3%', 'double', 'twice'. The value is the number as written (a minus only when the quote writes one). A written range in full ('$3–4 billion', 'between $3 billion and $4 billion', '$3 billion to $4 billion'), given as low and high; a change written 'from $3 billion to $5 billion' is two numbers, each copied alone. '$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%' in full, given as low and high or its midpoint as value. Only US dollars.\"}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'qualifier': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string', 'enum': ['none', 'approximately', 'as much as', 'more than', 'less than', 'estimated', 'at least', 'roughly', 'around', 'nearly', 'almost', 'up to', 'about', 'below', 'under', 'over', 'near', 'or more', 'or less'], 'description': \"Source only: the qualifier the quote writes just before the number (or 'or more' / 'or less' just after); none when there is none.\"}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'inputs': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': \"Computed only: ids of figures, never passages, in the operation's order.\"}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'operation': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string', 'enum': ['sum', 'difference', 'product', 'ratio', 'share', 'growth', 'apply_growth'], 'description': \"Computed only. sum(a, b, …) = a + b + … (one unit); difference(a, b) = a − b (one unit); product(a, b, …) = a × b × … (USD bn × x, x × x or % × x; never USD bn × %); ratio(a, b) = a ÷ b (same units give x; a ÷ x keeps a's unit); share(whole, percent) = whole × percent ÷ 100, the percent from 0 to 100; growth(old, new) = the % change, in one unit; apply_growth(base, rate %) = base × (1 + rate ÷ 100). sum and product take two or more inputs; the others exactly two. Never divide by a figure that can be zero. A range input gives a range: compute both extremes, a figure used twice taking one value; you may declare the midpoint as value. The figure equals the result within 0.5% (at least 0.1, or 0.05 for %). A sum never adds a figure of the part's quantity to one of the whole's for the same period (the whole already includes the part); a difference may take the part from the whole of the same period only to give the rest. A sum never adds one quantity for the same period twice. When a sum or difference combines periods of one quantity, write them FY2027, FY2027 Q3, FY2027 H1 or FY2027 Q1-Q3 (or CY likewise), and they make up the output's period exactly (Q1 + Q2 = H1; FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4).\"}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'basis_text': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string', 'description': 'Estimate only: the assumption, in words.'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'rests_on': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Estimate only: the ids of the figures and passages it rests on.'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'outcome_for': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['v29']}, 'description': \"The members whose forecast this figure is: your own forecast (a computed or estimate figure with basis forecast, even when it agrees with consensus), exactly one for each member answered as a forecast, none for an unresolved one. Its what is the member's outcome key, in USD bn.\"}, 'reference_for': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['v29']}, 'description': \"The members for which this figure is the market's reference. It and every figure beneath it is a source or a computed figure, never an estimate or a forecast, and at least one of them is a quoted consensus, guidance or outside figure. A past period's reported share or multiple carried to another period (a quarter's mix applied to the year) makes it our comparison estimate, not the market's reference.\"}}\nstructure dict_keys(['status', 'data', 'errors', 'recorded', 'published', 'decision', 'attempts'])\ndata {'figures': [{'id': 'F1', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investment commitments', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'as of 2026-07-26'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'reported', 'value': 25, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'evidence_id': 'e2620', 'quote_number': '$25 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'outcome_for': [], 'reference_for': []}, {'id': 'F2', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investment commitments for the remainder of the fiscal year', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'remainder of FY2027, as stated 2026-08-26'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'reported', 'value': 18, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'evidence_id': 'e2889', 'quote_number': '$18 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'outcome_for': [], 'reference_for': []}, {'id': 'F3', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'investment in OpenAI', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'announced late February; funding timing not specified'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'third_party', 'value': 30, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'evidence_id': 'e4486', 'quote_number': '$30 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'outcome_for': [], 'reference_for': []}, {'id': 'F4', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investments committed to ecosystem partners', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'period not specified; reported 2026-08-12'}, 'kind': 'source', 'basis': 'third_party', 'value': 70, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'evidence_id': 'e1732', 'quote_number': '$70 billion', 'qualifier': 'none', 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'basis_text': None, 'rests_on': None, 'outcome_for': [], 'reference_for': ['v29']}, {'id': 'F5', 'what': {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investment commitments', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'end of FY2027 (the balance at the end of FY2027, as the FY2027 annual report publishes it)'}, 'kind': 'estimate', 'basis': 'forecast', 'value': 45, 'low': None, 'high': None, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'evidence_id': None, 'quote_number': None, 'qualifier': None, 'inputs': None, 'operation': None, 'basis_text': \"My estimate is about $45 billion. The reported $25 billion balance and NVIDIA's statement that it had $18 billion committed for the remainder of the fiscal year indicate a gross scale around the low-$40 billions, but those are not additive measures of the ending balance: commitments may be fulfilled, and the $18 billion may overlap with transactions already discussed. I allow for some further commitments through FY2027, while not carrying the full $30 billion OpenAI investment forward as an incremental balance because it was announced in February and its funding timing and inclusion in the July balance are unclear. The higher alternative is supported by Bank of America's $70 billion estimate, but its period is unspecified and it does not map cleanly to the year-end outstanding balance. Jensen Huang's statement that large AI-lab investments were not expected to repeat next year also argues against assuming another large step-up.\", 'rests_on': ['F1', 'F2', 'F3', 'F4', 'e2643'], 'outcome_for': ['v29'], 'reference_for': []}], 'answers': [{'view_id': 'v29', 'shape': 'forecast', 'rung': 2, 'reference_unavailable': None, 'reasons': \"The reference available is Bank of America's $70 billion estimate, which sits on rung 3, but its period is unspecified, so it is a weak match for the end-FY2027 balance rather than a reason to forecast that rung. The more directly comparable company figure is the $25 billion commitment balance as of July 26; NVIDIA later described $18 billion committed for the remainder of its fiscal year. These support an outcome around the low-to-mid $40 billions before allowing for fulfillment, overlap, and some further commitments. The $30 billion OpenAI figure could push the outcome higher, but it was announced in February and the evidence does not establish that it is a new, outstanding commitment at FY2027 year-end. On balance, below $50 billion is more likely than at least $50 billion; my $45 billion estimate is on rung 2.\", 'why': None, 'cites': ['e2620', 'e2889', 'e4486', 'e1732', 'e2643'], 'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': []}]}\n\nLINE 6\nF2 $108.0 billion none Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\nF3 2% none Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\n\nLINE 10\nF3 $108.0 billion None Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\n\nLINE 14\nF1 $177,837 none Revenue\n$\n96,221\n$\n46,743\n$\n177,837\n$\n90,805\nF2 $108.0 billion none Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.\nF4 $392 billion none Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\n\nLINE 16\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
