a card (K...), passage (e...) or figure (F...) of this packet: usable: the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on; contradiction: with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction; internal_reference: the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation; deciding_gap: an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band\n1652 ## P19\n1653 ### Card K1: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n1685 For each card answer yes or no, each with a ground that names a card (K...), passage (e...) or figure (F...) of this packet: usable: the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on; contradiction: with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction; internal_reference: the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation; deciding_gap: an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band\n2356 ## P26\n2357 ### Card K1: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n2392 A\n2407 For each card answer yes or no, each with a ground that names a card (K...), passage (e...) or figure (F...) of this packet: usable: the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on; contradiction: with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction; internal_reference: the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation; deciding_gap: an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band\n2409 ## P27\n2410 ### Card K1: How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\n2456 For each card answer yes or no, each with a ground that names a card (K...), passage (e...) or figure (F...) of this packet: usable: the outcome is usable and supported by the 